{{!
    @template core/user_menu_metadata

    User menu metadata template, overridden by Dimensions.

    Modification compared to the original template:
    * Show the user's name beside the avatar in the navbar, from the md breakpoint up. Core renders
      only the avatar here and keeps the name inside the open menu; on a platform where people are
      addressed by rank, the name is what identifies the session at a glance. The name itself is
      core's, whatever fullname() composes under the site's fullnamedisplay setting.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * metadata - Array of extra badges (logged in as, failed logins), each with classes and content
    * avatardata - Array of avatars, each with classes and content
    * userfullname - The name of the logged in user

    Example context (json):
    {
        "metadata": [
            {
                "classes": "loginfailures",
                "content": "1 failed login attempt"
            }
        ],
        "avatardata": [
            {
                "classes": "current",
                "content": "<span class=\"userpicture\"></span>"
            }
        ],
        "userfullname": "Cel. Perovano"
    }
}}
{{#metadata}}
    <span class="usertext d-flex me-3">
        <span class="meta d-flex {{classes}}">
            {{{content}}}
        </span>
    </span>
{{/metadata}}
<span class="avatars">
    {{#avatardata}}
        <span class="avatar {{classes}}">
            {{{content}}}
        </span>
    {{/avatardata}}
</span>
{{#userfullname}}
    <span class="dimensions-usermenu-name d-none d-md-inline">{{userfullname}}</span>
{{/userfullname}}
